  "body": "### Summary\n\nTwo-line summary: LOT-057 (#83) reads the anonymous REST API on page 1 only, and treats every REST failure the same way (fallback to the HTML page), because nothing beyond `R57a`-`R57c` is captured. These anonymous GETs settle paging and the failure shapes.\n\n### Captures (anonymous, no account, read-only GETs; `R57*` naming and FIXTURES.md rules)\n\n1. `GET /webservices/rest_api.php?uri=forums/hardwarefr/categories/13/topics/last/&page=2`: does page 2 repeat the 5 sticky topics, and are `page` / `results_count` what page 1 says?\n2. The same with `&page=1&results_per_page=50`: is the parameter honoured (the HTML list shows 50 rows per page)?\n3. A page past the last one (`page=` ⌈`results_count` / 25⌉ + 1).\n4. An `/api/…` href requested as is, e.g. `GET /api/forums/hardwarefr/categories/` (redface2 E1 says 404; HFR-PROTOCOL §7: not tested).\n5. Error answers: an unknown category (`uri=forums/hardwarefr/categories/999/topics/last/`), an unknown topic (`…/categories/13/topics/999999999/`), and an unknown resource (`uri=forums/hardwarefr/nothing/`): status, content type, body.\n\nKeep each answer's status, headers (`Content-Type`, any `Set-Cookie` name) and bytes in the `.meta.json`, as for `R57a`-`R57c`.\n\n### Wanted by\n\nLOT-057 (#83): paging after page 1 and the per-failure rules (spec `docs/lots/LOT-057-rest-browsing.md`, pending capture). The logged-in flag buckets are #335, the sub-categories #285.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The five answers are in `Packages/HFRKit/Tests/HFRParsingTests/Fixtures/captures/` with their meta, anonymized and checked per FIXTURES.md.\n- [ ] HFR-PROTOCOL §6c LOT-057 updated with what they show.\n",
